<title>NORWAY: Transocean wins British contract.</title>
<headline>Transocean wins British contract.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian drilling and offshore services company Transocean ASA said on Tuesday Marathon Oil UK would lease mobile rig Transocean Explorer at considerably higher rates than today's.</p>
<p>Transocean, in a statement to the Oslo Bourse, gave no figures but said the contract was expected to take effect in April next year.</p>
<p>The deal covers four wells with an option for another well. It is expected to last 200 days with an option for another 40 days.</p>
<p>Transocean said Amoco had exercised an option for a six-month extension of the current 12-month leasing contract for Transocean Nordic. The rate is higher than the existing contract, Transocean said, again without giving any figures.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
